# BrandGuard AI — Cursor Rules

## Source of truth

Read and follow **`AGENTS.md`** before recommending or implementing changes.  
Design details live under **`docs/round-1/`**. Reusable workflows live in **`SKILLS.md`** (reference explicitly; not auto-loaded).

## Phase discipline

- Hackathon build window is open. Implement **one phase at a time** (see `docs/round-1/09-milestones.md`). Avoid building the entire project in a single operation.
- Prefer the P0 vertical slice over speculative infrastructure.
- A phase is incomplete until acceptance criteria and tests pass.

## Architecture invariants

- Hybrid review: deterministic validators + retrieval + structured LLM outputs.
- **Evidence gate:** citation IDs must be ⊆ the retrieval snapshot; fail closed.
- Statuses: `verified` | `contradicted` | `unsupported` | `indeterminate` | `policy_hit` | `suggestion_only`. Absence of evidence ≠ false.
- **Server-side authz** for roles and workflow transitions. UI checks are not authority.
- Never set content to `approved` because an LLM recommended it.
- No API secrets in client / `NEXT_PUBLIC_` for provider keys.
- **`LLM_MODEL` is always free:** `openrouter/free`, or a model id ending in `:free`. Do not set or suggest a paid id. Do not add a paid model as a fallback.
- Add `pgvector` only if retrieval evaluation justifies it.

## Engineering practice

- Prefer focused diffs aligned to the requested phase.
- Use Zod at trust boundaries (inputs, model outputs, transitions).
- Add or update tests for evidence gate, permissions, and claim-status behaviour when touching those areas.
- Do not invent metrics, user interviews, customers, or source citations.

## Completion

End substantive work with a short summary: files changed, tests, risks, next action.
